<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Chamdo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1950">1950</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Chamdo was fought in October 1950 in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-liberation-army">People's Liberation Army</a> crossed the Jinsha River and defeated the Tibetan army around the town of Chamdo, capturing the regional governor Ngapoi Ngawang Jigme. The defeat left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> without effective defences and led to the Seventeen Point Agreement of 1951, by which Tibet was incorporated into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-chamdo.jpg" alt="Battle of Chamdo" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 《人民画报》 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:195104_%E6%98%8C%E9%83%BD%E6%88%98%E5%BD%B9%E4%B9%8B%E5%89%8D%E8%A7%A3%E6%94%BE%E5%86%9B%E9%80%9A%E8%BF%87%E6%BE%9C%E6%B2%A7%E6%B1%9F.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…state signed a treaty of friendship and alliance with the Soviet Union and took Hainan, and after the <b>Battle of Chamdo</b> in October 1950 Tibet was incorporated under the Seventeen Point Agreement of 1951, completing control over almost all the mainland territory of the former Republic of China.</blockquote><a href="/empire/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In October 1950 the People's Liberation Army defeated the Tibetan army at <b>Chamdo</b>.</blockquote><a href="/state/tibet-1912-1951">Tibet (1912-1951)</a></li></ul></section>
